<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:35Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Spain: Housing crisis prompts general strike, mass nighttime protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b318487efa82dbc325ed3b62b4ada15a817d4d6071dda41b6cac0bbc16542f3f</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:23Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T21:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-housing-crisis-prompts-general-strike-mass-nighttime-protests/a-79915208--fc6d9d65a508.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-housing-crisis-prompts-general-strike-mass-nighttime-protests/a-79915208?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hundreds of thousands of citizens have hit the streets to protest Spain's housing crisis after millions of union workers staged a general strike. The crisis has triggered snap elections to take place on November 29.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fears of rising antisemitism in Europe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c40800e6a8262a0b718c3abb7dccf91c78eeff5ba81bf96ce3fbe65346b363b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:26Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T20:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783--20638e7d2425.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fears-of-rising-antisemitism-in-europe/a-79921783?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Holocaust survivor Regina Sluszny commemorates the victims of Auschwitz as Jewish communities across Europe face growing hostility. What does the promise of "Never Again" mean for Jewish life in Europe today?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>VW scraps production modernization plan citing tough financial straits</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aff584221ef19106370a51b9565c1d1fe1a8a8aeeed8322d2ba02071df694d64</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T19:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597--b06c676e46e8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/vw-scraps-production-modernization-plan-citing-tough-financial-straits/a-79923597?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">VW has announced that it will scrap large-scale modernization in light of its current economic situation. Employee representatives accuse leadership of putting short-term profits before long-term company viability.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Integration of immigrants in Germany: Much has been accomplished but problems remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a1d1873b56d0fffa15920fe7f471664e3563e7cc58ae399df352bf3b708ea31e</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:32Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241--cdefd1e9fff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/integration-of-immigrants-in-germany-much-has-been-accomplished-but-problems-remain/a-79923241?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Federal office for Migration and Refugees has released a new Integration Report. It found that while the integration of people with a migrant history is improving, violent youth remain a problem.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Democracy study: One-quarter of Germans want a right-wing authoritarian dictatorship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bad582463001cc0461c8717dc23c71697f94aea84cd7ab2e9d443e0b94439920</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:51:35Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718--e6377f13d887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/democracy-study-one-quarter-of-germans-want-a-right-wing-authoritarian-dictatorship/a-79922718?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The far-right AfD's electoral successes point to a new trend in Germany: Prejudice, resentment, and extremism are on the rise. A new study suggests satisfaction with democracy is at a low ebb.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya's last Ebola patient leaves hospital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fcdb819e734f9bbe064c82871311bdc60d137089b4dddc96e375391d732cf558</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T16:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-s-last-ebola-patient-leaves-hospital/a-79921240--e9705d91e6bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-s-last-ebola-patient-leaves-hospital/a-79921240?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Kenya had nine confirmed cases, while DR Congo continues to battle its deadliest outbreak of the disease.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil electoral court fines Meta, sees no deliberate election bias</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7ddf4a7388c56fbb1bd8b5bef9bba4714e79249c95894f02a37d895164ef10b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780--215a8f08f312.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/brazil-electoral-court-fines-meta-sees-no-deliberate-election-bias/a-79920780?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The fine came after President Lula's coalition filed a complaint. The court said there was no evidence of intent to influence the election. Meta said it will defend itself against "false allegations."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is AIIB's complaint mechanism failing affected communities?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61f30b78f6f3bacf1fcd9b3ace29991d8fcf0e8d392ea5e49b7d99c57cd14560</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917--1bfa788b7764.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-aiib-s-complaint-mechanism-failing-affected-communities/a-79919917?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AIIB has a grievance redress mechanism for people affected by projects it finances. But those seeking to file a complaint face significant hurdles. Critics say reforms and greater transparency are needed.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Wael Mohya could make German football history at 17</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dcd0aa94aaf588142d67854cb394175367706cba515d5636114e82b364cdd8ae</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T15:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787--677b2c671ea6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wael-mohya-could-make-german-football-history-at-17/a-79919787?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">At just 17, Gladbach forward Wael Mohya has earned his first Germany call-up. The dual-national talent has chosen the DFB path for now — and could soon make modern national-team history.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy: Hundreds of schools evacuated after bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:438280de9b236181b6e8401b26d2170cc922b600a0d8009dae239ec6e02d786d</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034--3d07ea5d3a16.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-hundreds-of-schools-evacuated-after-bomb-threats/a-79918034?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Although the government believes the threat to be a hoax, it has nevertheless prompted concerns about "hybrid warfare" in Europe. Similar messages were sent in Northern Ireland, Ireland, and Bulgaria.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tundu Lissu: After escaping the death penalty, what does his guilty verdict mean for Tanzania's democracy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f4a4cee16e59547ce6f0927a40ca8c80c7f927577d65dd59894b1bcbbc465df</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T13:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democr/a-79908512--3044020567d7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tundu-lissu-after-escaping-the-death-penalty-what-does-his-guilty-verdict-mean-for-tanzania-s-democracy/a-79908512?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A treason trial could have meant death by hanging for Tanzanian opposition leader Tundu Lissu. Instead, he now faces four years in prison for incitement to unrest. Can voices of dissident truly be heard in the country?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Only 1/3 of Germans satisfied with state of democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d4bf2b655edb2a83799cca1fabc3f32c4eb56db764911c047fcb3c4409f99b39</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066--348a315bae46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-only-1-3-of-germans-satisfied-with-state-of-democracy/live-79915066?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A new authoritarianism study has revealed a new low in satisfaction levels with the functioning of German democracy. Meanwhile, the Bundeswehr has banned Chinese-made drones. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran classes Argentina navy, air force as 'terrorist organizations'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9e4dc5d11a1eba15787f78a0b2e6f88955c7f999c2c0099f8211ac68cbfacf74</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-classes-argentina-navy-air-force-as-terrorist-organizations/a-79916290--7a72e35dd7c8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-classes-argentina-navy-air-force-as-terrorist-organizations/a-79916290?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In a tit-for-tat move, Iran has said it now considers Argentina's navy and air force as "terrorist organizations." Tehran claimed Buenos Aires is responsible for further consequences.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>DW Science explainer on the default mode network: what your brain does when you aren't focusing on anything, and why it's important.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1154dbbc900e4a695049d5621ab6f0c275fc7eabcfc8aacb6ae6b6a1fd061f9</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-an/a-79908787--cf91bcf53b1d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-science-explainer-on-the-default-mode-network-what-your-brain-does-when-you-aren-t-focusing-on-anything-and-why-it-s-important/a-79908787?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doing nothing might be the ultimate brain hack. When you're bored, the brain goes into default mode network. It's not only healthy for you, but it may also shape the very essence of your identity.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India: CPCB addresses stark Delhi pollution data gap on Diwali night</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:98d1320a890a8b1198fb6f6277369168bb182f6a9201995a1b88ae3d9e33abf5</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-cpcb-addresses-stark-delhi-pollution-data-gap-on-diwali-night/live-79914190--aefe747adc18.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-cpcb-addresses-stark-delhi-pollution-data-gap-on-diwali-night/live-79914190?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India's main pollution monitor has issued a clarification on a wide air quality data gap between official and private reporting in New Delhi that saw the city choked amid Diwali fireworks. DW has the latest.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany slips in climate protection rankings as other countries make gains</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:faf68ac92fded3d8e70a740d8d48c4aafe089c1ec6945519222dcb90ac87c8e3</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635--edb7d622928e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-slips-in-climate-protection-rankings-as-other-countries-make-gains/a-79913635?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Record renewable energy growth is driving climate progress in some countries, but Germany and many major emitters are falling behind.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>How AI worsens online violence against Middle East women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3f886c1775e99855a3b3e41a81ba536540530058125517e86b51bef935e649b</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T06:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-ai-worsens-online-violence-against-middle-east-women/a-79912634--666dfdf1ad89.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-ai-worsens-online-violence-against-middle-east-women/a-79912634?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women in the Middle East already have to deal with an above-average share of online harassment and violence. The proliferation of AI-enabled tools is making it worse.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea bus causes large crash near Seoul, dozens hurt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bce25d3f7ba91b5c35f3b7bd4b46cecfd85459fd0b5271044f39760901ff3a46</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T04:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-bus-causes-large-crash-near-seoul-dozens-hurt/a-79914074--7b0b10a102d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-bus-causes-large-crash-near-seoul-dozens-hurt/a-79914074?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bus triggered a collision involving more than 30 vehicles, including other buses, during rush hour traffic in the South Korean city of Seongnam, just south of Seoul.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel: Eisenkot proposes October 7 probe as new Knesset sworn in</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be2134f740b87db4b43c04c050085fd653dd6993eddd91a081f7b1c283998d69</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T03:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-eisenkot-proposes-october-7-probe-as-new-knesset-sworn-in/a-79913636--01a688ec8f46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-eisenkot-proposes-october-7-probe-as-new-knesset-sworn-in/a-79913636?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ex-IDF chief Gadi Eisenkot has yet to forge a coalition that would allow him to replace Benjamin Netanyahu, despite the new Knesset being dominated by the critics of the current prime minister.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US Republicans derail push to impeach Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a79f36273fb03f175bf5b4ba0e223f7c845d743214eb9df9ad6f2505deab051a</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-11T02:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-republicans-derail-push-to-impeach-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth/a-79913761--b41bf186f55b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-republicans-derail-push-to-impeach-defense-secretary-pete-hegseth/a-79913761?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Pentagon chief Pete Hegseth seems set to survive the impeachment bid launched by maverick Republican lawmaker Thomas Massie, with President Donald Trump praising the outcome of the vote.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US charges 3 alleged Iranian operatives over plots targeting Jewish communities and a UK airbase</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16c831a314a7f4b230a926096aa9c8df36a22f035a1d9fc314845aa85d3f05bd</id><updated>2026-11-11T22:50:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T23:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-charges-3-alleged-iranian-operatives-over-plots-targeting-jewish-communities-and-a-uk-airbase/a-79913543--477a23bfa03f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-charges-3-alleged-iranian-operatives-over-plots-targeting-jewish-communities-and-a-uk-airbase/a-79913543?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US prosecutors claim the three men were planning a "campaign of terror" against Jewish communities and a UK airbase. The Fairford incident prompted the US to pull out its bombers used for operations against Iran.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
